* text=auto eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Hook scripts must keep Unix line endings. The wildcard above already covers
# them, and this is written explicitly anyway: a shell script stored with CRLF
# often refuses to run, and a pre-push hook that refuses to run does not announce
# itself — it just stops guarding while everyone assumes it is there. The voice
# server repo hit exactly that on 2026-08-20 and carries the same rule.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
